Potree octree format
  The browser overlay reads Potree 2.0 octree files produced by the converter
  above. No Potree runtime source is copied into this repository.

npm dependencies
  Runtime and development dependencies are declared in package.json and
  pnpm-lock.yaml. Their licenses are permissive (MIT, ISC or Apache-2.0), for
  example: React, React DOM, Three.js, Radix UI icons, Lucide, mitt, fflate,
  clsx, tailwind-merge, class-variance-authority, Vite, Vitest, Playwright,
  TypeScript, ESLint, tsup and Tailwind CSS. Each dependency keeps its own
  license and copyright notice.

Python dependencies
  numpy and Pillow are used by the offline data tools (BSD-3-Clause and
  MIT-CMU respectively). The Waymo Open Dataset SDK is used through its
  published packages under Apache-2.0; it is a runtime dependency only and no
  Waymo code or data is redistributed here.

